# Down to the substrate: the oxide path to the neighbour is cut, the substrate path remains. Neighbour at 10 um.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Trench through cladding and buried oxide
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=80 ymin=-10 ymax=5
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 5
rect si -0.25 0.25 2 2.25
rect tin -1 1 4 4.25
heater h1 xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=4 ymax=4.25 power=0.1
probe wg1 xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
rect si 9.75 10.25 2 2.25
probe wg2 xmin=9.75 xmax=10.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
rect air 4 6 0 5
expect response wg1 h1 193.235287 1e-7
expect response wg2 h1 2.09480866 1e-7
expect pi_power wg1 h1 21.5626594 1e-7
expect peak 44.8381525 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 19200
